{"name":"Snakeskin","hex":"#786e61","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snakeskin","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The skin of a snake\n The hide of a snake, used as leather.\n The moult of a snake.","The hide of a snake, used as leather."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of snakeskin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snakeskin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snakeskin","blocks":[{"text":"Snakeskin may refer to the skin of a live snake, the shed skin of a snake after molting, or to a type of leather that is made from the hide of a dead snake. Snakeskin and scales can have varying patterns and color formations, providing protection via camouflage from predators. The colors and iridescence in these scales are largely determined by the types and amount of chromatophores located in the dermis of the snake skin. The snake's skin and scales are also an important feature to their locomotion, providing protection and minimizing friction when gliding over surfaces."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/HK_TKO_Tseung_Kwan_O_Plaza_mall_void_exhibition_%E9%83%8A%E9%87%8E%E9%81%8A_August_2022_Px3_04.jpg/330px-HK_TKO_Tseung_Kwan_O_Plaza_mall_void_exhibition_%E9%83%8A%E9%87%8E%E9%81%8A_August_2022_Px3_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snakeskin"},{"title":"Snakeskin (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Snakeskin is a 2001 New Zealand road thriller film directed by Gillian Ashurst and starring Melanie Lynskey. It was released theatrically in New Zealand on 11 October 2001. Despite not receiving an official release in the United States or the UK, it has played on television in both territories and amassed a cult following."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7b/Snakeskin_%282001%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snakeskin_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Iridescence_on_Garter_Snake_Scales.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Iridescence_on_Garter_Snake_Scales.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Iridescence_on_Garter_Snake_Scales.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Iridescence_on_Garter_Snake_Scales.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Iridescence_on_Garter_Snake_Scales.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Iridescence_on_Garter_Snake_Scales.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The large scutes on the right side cover the ventral, or belly side of the snake. The smaller scales cover the rest of the snake. Note how the scales overlap.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIridescence_on_Garter_Snake_Scales.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Dorsal_View_of_Snake_Scales.jpg/500px-Dorsal_View_of_Snake_Scales.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Dorsal_View_of_Snake_Scales.jpg/1280px-Dorsal_View_of_Snake_Scales.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Dorsal_View_of_Snake_Scales.jpg/500px-Dorsal_View_of_Snake_Scales.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The variation of scale colors as caused by different chromatophores, located on the dorsal (top) surface of a Garter snake.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADorsal_View_of_Snake_Scales.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Exposed_Garter_Snake_Integument.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Exposed_Garter_Snake_Integument.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&